{"id":"word:hebrew:H2859","type":"word","title":"חָתַן","subtitle":"H2859 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to give (a daughter) away in marriage ; hence (generally) to contract affinity by marriage","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָתַן (H2859) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 33 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָתַן (châthan) means to give (a daughter) away in marriage ; hence (generally) to contract affinity by marriage First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 3 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָתַן","transliteration":"châthan","pronunciation":"khaw-than'","strong":"H2859","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2859","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["חֹתֵ֣ן","חֹתֵ֥ן","לְ/הִתְחַתֵּ֖ן","חֹֽתְנ֗/וֹ","חֹתְנ֑/וֹ"],"morphs":[["HVqrmsc",10],["HVqrmsc/Sp3ms",8],["HC/Vtw3ms",2],["HR/Vtc",2],["HR/Vqrmsc/Sp3ms",2],["HVtp2ms",1],["HVtv2ms",1],["HVtc",1],["HVti2ms",1],["HVqrfsc/Sp3ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to give (a daughter) away in marriage ; hence (generally) to contract affinity by marriage","usage":"join in affinity, father in law, make marriages, mother in law, son in law.","full":"H2859. chathan חֹתֵן verbal noun 1. masculine wife's father (Arabic a circumciser , hence father-in-law, with reference to circumcision performed on young men just before marriage; relation on wife's side ; see We Prol. 1886, 355 Anm, 1; Skizzen iii, 154 Sta ZAW 1886. 143 Aum. Nö ZMG 1886, 187 ; otherwise Dl Pr 91 Lag BN 116 ) — construct חֹתֵן Exod 18:1 + 9t., חֹתֶנְךָ 18:6 , חֹתְנוֺ 3:1 + 9 t.; — usually of Moses' wife's father 3:1 ; 4:18 ; 18:1-2 , 5 , 6 , 7 , 8 , 12 (twice in verse); 18:14 ; 18:15 ; 18:17 ; 18:24 ; 18:27 (all E), Num 10:29 (J), Judg 1:16 ; 4:11 ; of a Levite 19:4 , 7 , 9 . 2. feminine wife's mother , only suffix חֹתַנְתּוֺ Deut 27:23 . II. חתן verb denominative only Hithpa`el make oneself a daughter's husband (Late Hebrew Hithpa`el id. , Aramaic Ithpa`al id. ) — Perfect 2masculine plural וְהִתְחַתַּנְתֶּם consecutive Josh 23:12 ; Imperfect וַיִּתְחַתֵּן 1Kin 3:1 ; 2Chr 18:1-2 ; masculine תִּתְחַתֵּן Deut 7:3 ; 1Sam 18:21 ; Imperative הִתְחַתֵּן 18:22 , הִתְחַתְּנוּ Gen 34:9 ; Infinitive הִתְחַתֵּן 1Sam 18:23 3 t.; — 1 make oneself daughter's husband (son-in-law) to, with בְּ 1Sam 18:21-22 , 23 , 26 , 27 ; with אֶת 1Kin 3:1 ; Gen 34:9 (P); with לְ 2Chr 18:1 , of marriage of Jehoshaphat's son and Ahab's daughter (compare 2Kin 8:18 2Chr 21:6 ). 2 in General form marriage-alliance with , with בְּ Deut 7:3 ; Josh 23:12 (D), Ezra 9:14 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 3 1","keyReferences":["1Kgs 3 1","1Sam 18 21","1Sam 18 22","1Sam 18 23","1Sam 18 26","1Sam 18 27","2Chr 18 1","Deut 7 3"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":33,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 3 1","book":"1Kgs","chapter":3,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּתְחַתֵּ֣ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vtw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 18 21","book":"1Sam","chapter":18,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּתְחַתֵּ֥ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtp2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 18 22","book":"1Sam","chapter":18,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִתְחַתֵּ֥ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtv2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 18 23","book":"1Sam","chapter":18,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִתְחַתֵּ֣ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtc"},{"reference":"1Sam 18 26","book":"1Sam","chapter":18,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/הִתְחַתֵּ֖ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vtc"},{"reference":"1Sam 18 27","book":"1Sam","chapter":18,"verse":27,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/הִתְחַתֵּ֖ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vtc"},{"reference":"2Chr 18 1","book":"2Chr","chapter":18,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּתְחַתֵּ֖ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vtw3ms"},{"refere